{"records":[{"id":"3ctpx4k6jp","title":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus upregulates SMPDL3B to promote viral replication by modulating lipid metabolism","description":"We generated a collection of porcine genome-scale CRISPR/Cas9 knockout (PigGeCKO) cells on a PAM background.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-26T18:53:54.241Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3ctpx4k6jp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3ctpx4k6jp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"huanh","last_name":"Shen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Agricultural Biotechnology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4g722x4jfg","title":"Western blot","description":"Western blot of CRISPR-Cas9-mediated nontargeting (NT) versus BACH2 knockout 3 days after CRISPR-Cas9-gRNA nucleofection of human gut cells.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-07-02T21:20:55.966Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4g722x4jfg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4g722x4jfg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yulong","last_name":"Wei","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gut","Western Blot","T Cell","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xv35nccf5g","title":"usp8 Meiding","description":"The CRISPR/Cas9 genome-editing tool was used to knock out the expression of USP8 (USP8-KO) in SUM159 cells. Knockout of USP8 was confirmed by western blot analysis using antibodies against USP8 and GAPDH. Raw data and raw data with molecular weigh labelled.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-04-30T20:10:51.846Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xv35nccf5g","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xv35nccf5g"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mei","last_name":"Ding","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nknd6w2kbm","title":"Supplementary information's for accepted manuscript in Cell press \"Star protocols\" :A Simple Method to Isolate a Single Human Cell PRDX1 Knockout Generated by CRISPR-Cas9 System","description":"Revised Supplementary information's for accepted manuscript in Cell press \"Star protocols\" :A Simple Method to Isolate a Single Human Cell PRDX1 Knockout Generated by CRISPR-Cas9 System","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-02-09T15:20:06.778Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nknd6w2kbm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nknd6w2kbm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mustapha","last_name":"Aouida","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Life Sciences","Cell Biology","Genetic Engineering","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"m8pkzbktbk","title":"Brunello Whole Genome Knock out library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells - NGS dataset of library population","description":"NGS data to confirm representative and balanced creation of the Brunello whole genome knock out library in BE(2)-C neuroblastoma cells. \nHuman Brunello CRISPR knockout pooled library was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #73178). \nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-11-01T07:40:29.578Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/m8pkzbktbk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/m8pkzbktbk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Genomic Library","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Knock Out","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"z4ht3txn2k","title":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023","description":"Accompanying Files for paper entitled: \"Genome-scale mapping of DNA damage suppressors through phenotypic CRISPR/Cas9 screens\" - Zhao et al. Molecular Cell 2023. This dataset contains Source and additional Data for all figures.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-06T07:16:19.286Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/z4ht3txn2k","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/z4ht3txn2k"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Daniel","last_name":"Durocher","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Yichao","last_name":"Zhao","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":null}],"categories":["DNA Replication","DNA Repair","Flow Cytometry","Cancer Chemotherapy","DNA Damage","Functional Genomics","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"33tm3dd9dw","title":"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery ","description":"Raw data deposited for \"FAME-CRISPR: Improved CRISPR-Cas9 Genome Editing via HDAC Inhibition and Engineered Virus-Like Particle Delivery\" by Djamshidi et al-Cell Reports Methods","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-09-25T15:53:30.358Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/33tm3dd9dw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/33tm3dd9dw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahbod","last_name":"Djamshidi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Sanger Sequencing","Immunofluorescence"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"cszpw4c66t","title":"Structural insights into Cas9-mediated prespacer selection in CRISPR-Cas adaptation. Gaizauskaite et al.","description":"During CRISPR-Cas adaptation, prokaryotic cells become immunized by the insertion of foreign DNA fragments, termed spacers, into the host genome to serve as templates for RNA-guided immunity. Spacer acquisition relies on the Cas1-Cas2 integrase and accessory proteins, which select DNA sequences flanked by the protospacer adjacent motif (PAM) and insert them into the CRISPR array. It has been shown that in type II-A systems selection of PAM-proximal prespacers is mediated by the effector nuclease Cas9, which forms a ‘supercomplex’ with the Cas1-Cas2 integrase and the Csn2 protein. Here, we present cryo-electron microscopy structures of the type II-A prespacer selection supercomplex in the DNA-scanning and two distinct PAM-bound configurations, providing insights into the mechanism of Cas9-mediated prespacer selection in type II-A CRISPR-Cas systems. Repurposing of Cas9 by the CRISPR adaptation machinery for prespacer selection characterized here demonstrates Cas9 plasticity and expands our knowledge of the Cas9 biology.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-02-20T09:45:34.481Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/cszpw4c66t","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/cszpw4c66t"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ugne","last_name":"Gaizauskaite","orcid":"0009-0008-9137-5428"},{"first_name":"Giedre","last_name":"Tamulaitiene","orcid":"0000-0002-9794-3544"},{"first_name":"Arunas","last_name":"Silanskas","orcid":"0000-0002-6385-6928"},{"first_name":"Giedrius","last_name":"Gasiunas","orcid":"0000-0003-2509-9054"},{"first_name":"Virginijus","last_name":"Siksnys","orcid":"0000-0003-1983-2096"},{"first_name":"Giedrius","last_name":"Sasnauskas","orcid":"0000-0002-3185-2682"}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/02gs16m83","name":"Lietuvos Mokslo Taryba","grant_id":"S-MIP-19-32"}],"categories":["Biochemistry"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":107487,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":100,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":107487,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":107025,"restricted":53,"embargoed":409},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1869},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":565},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":424},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":366},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":362},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":359},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":330},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":293},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":234},{"id":"https://ror.org/00k4n6c32","name":"European Commission","count":193}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":104975},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1884},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":168},{"id":"b07018a5-fee